{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaFpxUfQujEJphsv1n1q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 01 is done. The census is the new \"Pebbling\" section at the end of `paper2/equivalences.md`, and the gate passes (`lake build` ok, 1 `sorry` against a limit of 1, 1,231 tests passed). As the item required, it has no Lean and no Python.\n\n**Verdict:** progressive black-white pebbling relates to vertex separation exactly, so it belongs in the complex. The offset depends on which graph the game is played against:\n\n- **KP Thm 3.1, combined with their Thm 4.1:** `mpb = mpbw = pw + 1` on every nonempty graph, using the graph itself. That is the same offset as interval thickness and narrowness, and it is the natural thirteenth member.\n- **Lengauer Thm 2:** `pbw(D) = pw(D_u) + 1` on every nonempty dag D. This is also exactly the open-stacks value of a matrix with one column per vertex v, holding v and its immediate predecessors, because D_u is that matrix's MOSP graph.\n- **Lengauer Thm 3:** `pbw(G_d) = pw(G) + 2` for any graph with an edge.\n- **Not a member:** the unrestricted game (recomputation allowed) needs at most 3 pebbles on every G_d.\n\n**Faults and edge cases in the sources:**\n- KP Thm 3.1's `mpb = ns` is false on edgeless graphs: `ns = 0` but `mpb = 1`.\n- Lengauer Thm 2's yes/no form fails at K = 1 on edgeless dags, because his vertex separator game (VSG) requires K ≥ 1. It holds if you use vertex separation (vs) instead. Thm 3's yes/no form then holds for every K ≥ 0.\n- Lengauer's remark (p. 467) that recomputation doesn't help on directed trees is refuted, for trees directed root to leaves, by KP's own ternary-tree example. It can only be true for trees directed towards the root.\n- KP's claim of \"no recontamination\" in one proof step is true but given without argument. The census writes out the argument.\n\n**Observations the sources don't make:**\n- The undirected graphs of the form D_u are exactly the chordal graphs. That is why Lengauer needs the detour through G_d for Thm 3.\n- `mpb = mpbw = pw + 1` has short direct proofs that avoid the search-game monotonicity theorems.\n\nI checked every relation above with a throwaway script in /tmp, which is not item 02's checker. It found no failures:\n- on all dags up to 5 vertices;\n- on all graphs up to 5 vertices;\n- for Thm 3, on graphs where vertices plus edges total at most 9.\n\nSection P.5 lists the eight statements for item 02 to check properly, and P.6 sketches the Lean route for items 03–04. PROGRESS.md (now 1/13) and iterations.md are updated; nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1898,"cache_read_input_tokens":128950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1898,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ec40a5-6ca1-460c-bb76-e8db9cb9654e","uuid":"60ffaa52-ece9-40cf-b33d-5a657dfe2138","timestamp":"2026-09-30T20:29:38.026Z","request_id":"req_011CfaFpx1dzyy4StPi2ste4"}
